# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows normally converts files to CRLF on checkout, which is harmless for C# and fatal for a
# shell script: a CRLF shebang makes Linux report "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" and refuse to
# run it. Since the server is built and deployed on Linux, publish.sh has to survive a checkout made on
# Windows, so its line endings are pinned here rather than left to whatever each machine prefers.
#
# Batch files are pinned the other way for the same reason in reverse: cmd.exe is unreliable with LF.

*.sh text eol=lf

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
